posts/c&c++/c++2.0/14 shared_ptr.html.body:
智能指针
使用传统的指针手动管理内存，会存在以下等问题：

Memory leaks: If you forget to call delete, dynamically allocated memory is not freed.
Dangling pointers: If you call delete but continue using the pointer, you can access freed memory, leading to undefined behavior.
Double deletions: Deleting the same memory twice can lead to undefined behavior, often causing crashes or corruption of memory.
Exception unsafe: 在抛出异常的情况下，使用指针管理的内存会有内存泄露的可能。异常栈在展开时不会释放指针管理的内存。

c++11提供的智能指针，旨在提供以下的功能：

Automatic Resource Management
ensure that resources are properly cleaned up when they are no longer needed
Exception Safety
在抛出异常的情况下，使用智能指针管理的内存也会被合适的处理，需要释放的时候会被释放。

shared_ptr
//defined in header 
template
class shared_ptr;

其类型成员(using)
element_type     std::remove_extent_t    

weak_type     std::weak_ptr
其中remove_extext_t
template
using remove_extent_t = typename remove_extent::type;

template
struct remove_extent { using type = T; };

template
struct remove_extent { using type = T; };

template
struct remove_extent { using type = T; };

主要功能
Allows shared ownership of a resource. Multiple shared_ptrs can manage the same resource, and the resource is automatically freed when the last shared_ptr goes out of scope 
内部实现
一个shared_ptr的实现，包括两个指针

the stored pointer (one returned by get())
a pointer to control block

control block中含有如下

either a pointer to the managed object or the managed object itself
the deleter (type-erased)
the allocator (type-erased) 
the number of shared_ptrs that own the managed object
the number of weak_ptrs that refer to the managed object

stored_pointer
stored_pointer是用于alias constructor的，详见后文。
control block

either a pointer to the managed object or the managed object itself
如果我们构造shread_ptr是传递的已经构造好的对象的指针，这个指针就被存储到这里。当我们使用make_shared创建shared_ptr时，如果对象很小，make_shared可能就会使用in-place allocation,将对象直接创建在control block中。这叫sso(small object optimilization), 既减少了内存分配的次数，也可以避免小对象造成的内存碎片。
比如std::shared_ptr ptr(new int(42)); 我们直接new好了对象，再将对象传递给shared_ptr管理，虽然int很小，但不会被sso优化。而如果是std::shread_ptr ptr = std::make_shared(42);，这时候，对象的分配就可能会使用sso优化，直接分配在control block中。
the deleter (type-erased)
这个是在最后一个shared_ptr goes out of scope 后释放对象时需要调用的析构函数。之所以是type_erased，是为了在shared_ptr可以在clean up object时，不需要知道对象的类型。这在有继承的情况下非常有用。比如shared_ptr管理的是派生对象Derived,而Base中的析构函数不是virtual的，这时候在对象析构时，一样能正确的调用到派生对象的析构函数。而unique_ptr就做不到了。unique_ptr这时候就会只调用Base的析构函数。
type-erased deleter通常使用void (*)(void*) 函数指针，其中的参数是void*的，任何类型的对象指针都可以转换成void*。当然，我们也可以在构造时传递自己的deleter,只要是任何符合签名的可调用对象即可。（任何类型都可以转换成void*，所以对类型没有要求）
the allocator (type-erased) 
The allocator is an optional component in std::shared_ptr that allows you to specify the memory allocation strategy for the managed object. By default, std::shared_ptr uses the global ::opereator new ()for memory allocation, but you can provide a custom allocator to control how memory is allocated and deallocated for the managed object.
Similar to the deleter, the allocator is type-erased. The type-erasure mechanism allows std::shared_ptr to store a generic allocator that can allocate memory for any type of object. The allocator is usually a callable object that has an allocate() and  deallocate() methods.
Example
#include 
#include 

template 
struct MyAllocator {
    using value_type = T;

    MyAllocator() = default;

    template  
    MyAllocator(const MyAllocator&) {}

    T* allocate(std::size_t n) {
        std::cout (::operator new(n * sizeof(T)));
    }

    void deallocate(T* ptr, std::size_t n) {
        std::cout  ptr = std::allocate_shared(MyAllocator(), 42);
    return 0;
}

Output
Custom allocating 1 elements
Custom deallocating 1 elements

the number of shared_ptrs that own the managed object
The destructor of shared_ptr decrements the number of shared owners of the control block. If that counter reaches zero, the control block calls the destructor of the managed object. The control block does not deallocate itself until the std::weak_ptr counter reaches zero as well.
the number of weak_ptrs that refer to the managed object
这个值在control block被创建时初始化为1，而后如果有weak_ptr weak reference this object,这个值会加1. 当最后一个shared_ptr dead时，会减1.
也就是number of weak_ptrs, plus 1 if there are any shared_ptrs outstanding。This can be understood as the number of things that are keeping the control block alive。
Doing it this way (instead of store this number as shread_ptrs+weak_ptrs) allows shared_ptr operations to avoid uselessly modifying the weak refcount ，it will simply be initialized to 1 and decremented by 1 upon the death of the last shared_ptr. if no weak_ptrs then, the number will be zero， the control block will be released.
还有另一种实现思路，这里只存储weak_ptrs的个数，不加一。那这时候判断是否需要释放control block就需要加锁了。比较容易出错。

使用
