Creates a new std::shared_ptr that shares ownership of the managed object. If there is no managed object, i.e. this is empty, then the returned shared_ptr also is empty.
Effectively returns `expired() ? shared_ptr() : shared_ptr(this)`, executed atomically.
Both this function and the constructor of std::shared_ptr using std::weak_ptr needs to  acquire temporary ownership of the managed object referred to by the std::weak_ptr. The difference is that the constructor of std::shared_ptr throws an exception when its std::weak_ptr argument is empty, while std::weak_ptr::lock() constructs an empty std::shared_ptr.
