posts/c&c++/exceptional c++/item24.html.body:
"Is implemented in terms of"的语义有两种实现方式，nonpublic inheritance 和 Containment，如下
// Example 1
//
template 
class MyList
{
public:
    bool Insert( const T&, size_t index );
    T Access( size_t index ) const;
    size_t Size() const;
private:
    T* buf_;
    size_t bufsize_;
};


// Example 1(a)
//
template 
class MySet1 : private MyList
{
public:
    bool Add( const T& ); // calls Insert()
    T Get( size_t index ) const;// calls Access()
    using MyList::Size;
    //...
};


// Example 1(b)
//
template 
class MySet2
{
public:
    bool Add( const T& ); // calls impl_.Insert()
    T Get( size_t index ) const; // calls impl_.Access()
    size_t Size() const; // calls impl_.Size();
    //...
private:
    MyList impl_;
};


nonpublic inheritance 主要实现的是 " IS-IMPLEMENTED-IN-TERMS-OF" 的语义, 同时还可以实现"controlled polymorphyism"的语义。派生类可以使用基类的public 和protected parts
Containment 表达的是 HAS-A  关系，也就是也是实现的 "IS-IMPLEMENTED-IN-TERMS-OF"的语义，但是 using class只能使用 used class的public部分

Guideline : When modeling IS-IMPLEMENTED-IN-TERMS-OF, always prefer expressing it using containment, not inheritance.
那么，什么时候prefer nonpublic inheritance over containment? 

需要override virtual function.尤其是，如果used class is abstract
需要访问protected member,尤其是访问protected contructors
We need to construct the used object before, or destroy it after, another base subobject. If the slightly longer object lifetime matters, there's no way to get it other than by using inheritance. This can be necessary when the used class provides a lock of some sort, such as a critical section or a database transaction, which must cover the entire lifetime of another base subobject.
We need to share a common virtual base class or override the construction of a virtual base class. The first part applies if the using class has to inherit from one of the same virtual bases as the used class. If it does not, the second part may still apply. The most-derived class is responsible for initializing all virtual base classes, so if we need to use a different constructor or different constructor parameters for a virtual base, then we must inherit.
如果used class是empty class, 只有函数成员，没有数据成员，这时候，继承 used class编译器可能会应用empty base class优化，也就是基类不占有空间。而如果是containment,即使是空对象，也最起码要占有一个byte. 但需要注意的是，并不是所有的编译器都会应用 empty base class优化。即使编译器有empty base class优化，除非内存使用对你的程序很重要，并且这样的对象在运行中会创建很多，比如tens of thousands， 那么这时候， inheritance是个不错的选择，否则，inheritance means stronger relationship than simple containment
inheritance 除了能实现IS-IMPLEMENTED-IN-TERMS-OF的语义之外，还可以实现 controlled polymorphism 的语义，而这个多态性，是被控制在派生类的内部，友元，以及派生类的派生类这些范围之内。
Public inheritance should always model IS-A as per the Liskov Substitution Principle (LSP).Nonpublic inheritance can express a restricted form of IS-A, even though most people identify IS-A with public inheritance alone. Given class Derived : private Base, from the point of view of outside code, a Derived object IS-NOT-A Base. So, of course, it can't be used polymorphically as a Base because of the access restrictions imposed by private inheritance. However, inside Derived's own member functions and friends only, a Derived object can indeed be used polymorphically as a Base (you can supply a pointer or reference to a Derived object where a Base object is expected), because members and friends have the necessary access. If instead of private inheritance, you use protected inheritance, then the IS-A relationship is more visible to further-derived classes, which means subclasses can also make use of the polymorphism.

最后，什么时候应该使用public inheritance? when we  need public inheritance to express IS-A
对于给出的 MySet的两个实现，我们分析下nonpublic inheritance是不是必要的？

MyList has no protected members, so we don't need to inherit to gain access to them.
MyList has no virtual functions, so we don't need to inherit to override them.
MySet has no other potential base classes, so the MyList object doesn't need to be constructed before, or destroyed after, another base subobject.
MyList has no virtual base classes that MySet might need to share or whose construction it might need to override.
MyList is nonempty, so the "empty base class optimization" motive does not apply.
MySet IS-NOT-A MyList, not even within MySet's member functions and friends. 

In short, MySet should not inherit from MyList. 
containment的优点，除了降低类与类之间的依赖，降低耦合性之外，it  also allows having multiple instances of the used class,除此之外， containment 还可以实现 compiler firewall using Pimpl. 最后，对于MySet的containment实现，我们可以实现一个更为泛型的版本
// Example 1(c): Generic containment
//
template  >
class MySet3
{
public:
  bool Add( const T& ); // calls impl_.Insert()
  T Get( size_t index ) const;
  // calls impl_.Access()
  size_t Size() const; // calls impl_.Size();
  // ...
private:
  Impl impl_;
};

这时候，MySet 的used class不只是 MyList, 任何实现了Insert,Access,Size函数的类型都可以被作为模板参数。标准库中的stack和queue就是如此设计的。这种泛化的实现，在使用时，根据client的不同需求，比如如果有的client需要insert多于search,这时候可选择insert优化的 Impl具体类型。
This kind of flexibility is more difficult to achieve with inheritance, primarily because inheritance tends to fix an implementation decision at design time. 
最后，对于public inheritance: 
Only use public inheritance to model true IS-A, as per the Liskov Substitution Principle. That is, a publicly derived class object should be able to be used in any context in which the base class object could be used and still guarantee the same semantics. 
Guideline : Always ensure that public inheritance models both IS-A and WORKS-LIKE-A according to the Liskov Substitution Principle. All overridden member functions must require no more and promise no less.
Guideline : Never inherit publicly to reuse (code in the base class); inherit publicly in order to be reused (by existing code that uses base objects polymorphically).
Conclusion
Use inheritance wisely. If you can express a class relationship using containment/delegation alone, you should always prefer that. If you need inheritance but aren't modeling IS-A, use nonpublic inheritance. If you don't need the combinative power of multiple inheritance, prefer single inheritance. Large inheritance hierarchies, in general, and deep ones, in particular, are confusing to understand and therefore difficult to maintain. Inheritance is a design-time decision and trades off a lot of run-time flexibility. Some people feel that "it just isn't OO unless you inherit," but that isn't really true. Use the simplest solution that works, and you'll be more likely to enjoy many pleasant years of stable and maintainable code.
