posts/c&c++/exceptional c++/item26.html.body:
降低compile-time dependencies
假设有如下头文件
// x.h: original header
//
#include 
#include 
#include 
// None of A, B, C, D or E are templates.
// Only A and C have virtual functions.
#include "a.h" // class A
#include "b.h" // class B
#include "c.h" // class C
#include "d.h" // class D
#include "e.h" // class E
class X : public A, private B
{
public:
X( const C& );
B f( int, char* );
C f( int, C );
C& g( B );
E h( E );
virtual std::ostream& print( std::ostream& ) const;
private:
std::list clist_;
D d_;
};
inline std::ostream& operator
如果client需要包含这个头文件使用X,那么该文件的compile-time dependencies如何降低？也就是如果更改该文件，或者更改该文件#include进来的文件，尽量降低client重新编译的时间？

remove #include 
replace ostream with iosfwd

iosfwd中包含的是ostream的前置名声，而ostream中包含的是ostream的完整定义，我们这个头文件中仅仅使用ostream作为函数参数和返回值类型，只需要前置声明即可。那么，我们是否可以直接写class ostream，而不用#include 呢？在很久以前是可以的，那时候，ostream只是个class类型，并且不在namespace std中。现在不行了，ostream现在在std namespace中，程序员不允许声明std中已经存在的类型。并且现在ostream也不再是class了，而是typedef'd as basic_ostream。 The standard library helpfully provides the header iosfwd, which contains forward declarations for all the stream templates (including basic_ostream) and their standard typedefs (including ostream). So all we need to do is replace "#include " with "#include ".
Guideline. Prefer to #include  when a forward declaration of a stream will suffice.
Incidentally, once you see iosfwd, one might think that the same trick would work for other standard library templates, such as list and string. There are, however, no comparable "stringfwd" or "listfwd" standard headers. The iosfwd header was created to give streams special treatment for backward compatibility, to avoid breaking code written in years past for the "old" nontemplated version of the iostreams subsystem.

Replace e.h with a forward declaration

class E在当前文件中仅仅被作为参数和返回值类型，因此可使用前置声明而不是include头文件。
Guideline : Never #include a header when a forward declaration will suffice.
那么 class A, class B能不能被前置声明呢？不能。 因为X继承自A,B. 编译器需要确定X object的大小，virtual functions, and other fundamentals. 因此需要 A和B的完整定义。
那么 class C, class D呢？也不能。 because a list and a D appear as private data members of X. Although C appears as neither a base class nor a member, it is being used to instantiate the list member, and most current compilers require that when you instantiate list, you are able to see the definition of C. 同时，如果编译器需要知道X object的大小，肯定是需要知道其data member的类型的完整定义。
现在这个头文件被优化成如下
// x.h: sans gratuitous headers
//
#include 
#include 
// None of A, B, C or D are templates.
// Only A and C have virtual functions.
#include "a.h" // class A
#include "b.h" // class B
#include "c.h" // class C
#include "d.h" // class D
class E;
class X : public A, private B
{
public:
X( const C& );
B f( int, char* );
C f( int, C );
C& g( B );
E h( E );
virtual std::ostream& print( std::ostream& ) const;
private:
std::list clist_;
D d_;
};

inline std::ostream& operator
还可以进一步降低编译依赖么？可以的。使用pimpl实现compiler firewall.
虽然client code是不可以访问X的private part的，也就是不可以访问X的implementation detail。 然而，X 的implementation detail却声明在头文件中。当client code include x.h后，X 的implementation detail的任何改动，都将导致client code重新编译。比如当前的实现，不管是X本身private part的任何改动，还是 C, D class 的任何改动，都将导致最终client code被重新编译。
How can we better insulate clients from a class's private implementation details?
using pimpl idiom as a compilation firewall . A Pimpl is just an opaque pointer (a pointer to a forward-declared, but undefined, helper class) used to hide the private members of a class. 
// file x.h
class X
{
  // public and protected members
private:
  struct XImpl;
  XImpl* pimpl_;
  // a pointer to a forward-declared class
};

// file x.cpp
struct X::XImpl
{
  // private members; fully hidden, can be
  // changed at will without recompiling clients
};

The major advantages of this idiom come from the fact that it breaks compile-time dependencies.

Types mentioned only in a class's implementation need no longer be defined for client code, which can eliminate extra #includes and improve compile speeds.
A class's implementation can be changed—that is, private members can be freely added or removed, without recompiling client code. If in client code ,we create that class object, there's only a pointer in it, the change of implementation doesn't affect client code .

The major costs of this idiom are in performance.

Each construction/destruction must allocate/deallocate memory.
Each access of a hidden member can require at least one extra indirection. 

Guideline:
For widely used classes, prefer to use the compiler-firewall idiom (Pimpl Idiom) to hide implementation details. Use an opaque pointer (a pointer to a declared, but undefined, class) declared as "struct XxxxImpl; XxxxImpl* pimpl_;" to store private members (including both state variables and member functions)
使用pimpl优化后的头文件如下
// x.h: after converting to use a Pimpl
//
#include 
#include "a.h" // class A (has virtual functions)
#include "b.h" // class B (has no virtual functions)
class C;
class E;
class X : public A, private B
{
public:
  X( const C& );
  B f( int, char* );
  C f( int, C );
  C& g( B );
  E h( E );
  virtual std::ostream& print( std::ostream& ) const;
private:
  struct XImpl;
  XImpl* pimpl_;
  // opaque pointer to forward-declared class
};
inline std::ostream& operator
The private details go into X's implementation file, where client code never sees them and therefore never depends upon them.
// Implementation file x.cpp
//
struct X::XImpl
{
std::list clist_;
D d_;
};

还可以继续优化么？
我们注意到class B是 private继承的，也就是实现的是is implemented in terms of 的语义，之前说过，这样的语义有两种实现方式，nonpublic inheritance 和 containment
之前列举了需要使用nonpublic继承的几种情况，其中比较常见的是class B有virtual function, 而我们的类需要重写virtual function. 这里注释中说明了class B 没有virtual function, 所以很可能nonpublic inheritance不是必须的。（当然还有其他的理由，这里假设都不满足）。这时候，如果containment可以满足is implemented in terms of 的语义时，就应该使用这种实现方式降低耦合性。
应用这种优化之后，b.h的头文件也可以被省去了。Because the B member object should be private (it is, after all, an implementation detail), this member should live in X's hidden pimpl_ portion.
// x.h: after removing unnecessary inheritance
//
#include 
#include "a.h" // class A
class B;
class C;
class E;
class X : public A
{
public:
X( const C& );
B f( int, char* );
C f( int, C );
C& g( B );
E h( E );
virtual std::ostream& print( std::ostream& ) const;
private:
struct XImpl;
XImpl* pimpl_; // this now quietly includes a B
};
inline std::ostream& operator
Guideline : Never inherit when composition is sufficient.
