Although the program text is semantically correct, it is not yet instructionally correct. Next we must generate temporaries to hold the return values of our function calls:

Generate a temporary of class X to hold the return value of getValue() :X temp1 = xx.getValue();


Generate a temporary of class Y to hold the return value of operator Y() :Y temp2 = temp1.operator Y();


Generate a temporary of type bool to hold the return value of the equality operator:bool temp3 = yy.operator==( temp2 );


