Although a void* is guaranteed to be big enough to hold the value of any object pointer, it is not guaranteed to be suitable to hold a function pointer. On some platforms, a function pointer is larger than an object pointer. Even if code like above happens to work on the compiler you’re using today, it’s not portable and may not work on another compiler, or even on the next release of your current compiler.

