Normally, a special-purpose FuncPtr proxy class like this (which contains some old object and doesn’t really care much about its type) just cries out to be templatized into a general-purpose Holder proxy. Alas, you can’t just directly templatize the FuncPtr class above, because then the typedef would have to look something like the following,typedef Holder (*FuncPtr)(); which is self-referential.

